IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sg-periods`

-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition: ss 12B to 12D -- correcting a register: by the Court (12B), by the Registrar on an officer's notice (12C),
-- and by the Registrar on its own initiative (12D), with the notice, objection and bar that protect the company or person. Layer 1 (the law, objectively).
-- The Registrar and the Court appear only as the holders of powers and duties over the individual; there is no seat for them.
--
-- Answers. `JUST TRUE` is yes; `JUST FALSE` is the text saying no in its own words; `NOTHING` is "the text does not say".
-- Periods are counted only by sg-periods.l4. "within N days after X" in a duty or a right is read here as: X itself is in time (fork line F-H-P2 in NOTES.md).

§ `Section 12B: rectification by the Court`

-- "Where it appears to the Court, as a result of evidence adduced before it by an applicant company, that any particular recorded in a register is erroneous or defective, the Court may, by order, direct":
-- a grant gated by "Where": JUST FALSE when the gate fails (periods ruling (b); split site (ii), fork line F-H-S1).
-- src:3056 | 12B.—(1) Where it appears to the Court, as a result of evidence
-- src:3057 | adduced before it by an applicant company, that any particular
-- src:3058 | recorded in a register is erroneous or defective, the Court may, by
-- src:3059 | order, direct the Registrar to rectify the register on such terms and
-- src:3060 | conditions as seem to the Court just and expedient, as are specified in
-- src:3061 | the order and the Registrar must, upon receipt of the order, rectify the
-- src:3062 | register accordingly.
@ref s 12B(1) (src:3056-3062)
GIVEN `evidence was adduced before the Court by an applicant company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it appears to the Court, as a result of that evidence, that a particular recorded in a register is erroneous or defective` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 12B(1) the Court may by order direct the Registrar to rectify the register` MEANS
    IF `evidence was adduced before the Court by an applicant company` AND `it appears to the Court, as a result of that evidence, that a particular recorded in a register is erroneous or defective`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where it appears to the Court, as a result of evidence adduced before it by an applicant company, that any particular recorded in a register is erroneous or defective, the Court may, by order, direct the Registrar to rectify the register" (a failed "where": the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (b); split site (ii), fork line F-H-S1)

-- src:3056 | 12B.—(1) Where it appears to the Court, as a result of evidence
-- src:3057 | adduced before it by an applicant company, that any particular
-- src:3058 | recorded in a register is erroneous or defective, the Court may, by
-- src:3059 | order, direct the Registrar to rectify the register on such terms and
-- src:3060 | conditions as seem to the Court just and expedient, as are specified in
-- src:3061 | the order and the Registrar must, upon receipt of the order, rectify the
-- src:3062 | register accordingly.
@ref s 12B(1) (src:3056-3062)
GIVEN `the Registrar has received an order of the Court under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 12B(1) the Registrar must rectify the register accordingly` MEANS
    IF `the Registrar has received an order of the Court under subsection (1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the Registrar must, upon receipt of the order, rectify the register accordingly" (a failed "upon": counts as "where", the delegated-defences ruling of 2026-11-05, item (c); a duty's own question)

-- src:3066 | (2) An order of the Court made under subsection (1) may require
-- src:3067 | that a fresh document, showing the rectification, must be filed by the
-- src:3068 | applicant company with the Registrar together with a copy of the
-- src:3069 | Court order, and a copy of the Court application.
@ref s 12B(2) (src:3066-3069)
GIVEN `the order of the Court under subsection (1) requires that a fresh document, showing the rectification, be filed by the applicant company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 12B(2) the applicant company must file the fresh document with the Registrar together with a copy of the Court order and a copy of the Court application` MEANS
    IF `the order of the Court under subsection (1) requires that a fresh document, showing the rectification, be filed by the applicant company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An order ... may require that a fresh document ... must be filed"; the duty arises only if the order requires it, and the text says nothing of an order that does not

§ `Section 12C: rectification by the Registrar on an officer's notice`

-- src:3073 | 12C.—(1) Despite section 12B, an officer of a company may notify
-- src:3074 | the Registrar in the prescribed form of —
-- src:3076 | (a) any error contained in any document relating to the
-- src:3077 | company filed or lodged with the Registrar; or
-- src:3079 | (b) any error in the filing or lodgment of any document
-- src:3080 | relating to the company with the Registrar.
@ref s 12C(1) (src:3073-3080)
GIVEN `the person is an officer of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the error is an error contained in a document relating to the company filed or lodged with the Registrar` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the error is an error in the filing or lodgment of a document relating to the company with the Registrar` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notification is in the prescribed form` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 12C(1) the officer of the company may notify the Registrar of the error` MEANS
    IF    `the person is an officer of the company`
      AND (`the error is an error contained in a document relating to the company filed or lodged with the Registrar` OR `the error is an error in the filing or lodgment of a document relating to the company with the Registrar`)
      AND `the notification is in the prescribed form`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an officer of a company may notify the Registrar in the prescribed form of (a) any error contained in any document relating to the company ...; or (b) any error in the filing or lodgment"; the text says nothing of another person, another error or another form

-- "The Registrar may, upon receipt of any notification referred to in subsection (1) and if satisfied that (a) ... or (b) ..., rectify the register accordingly":
-- "upon receipt" counts as "where" (delegated-defences ruling (c)), so no notification is JUST FALSE (split site (ii), fork line F-H-S1); "if satisfied" is an "if" gate on a grant, so a notification the Registrar is not satisfied about is NOTHING (fork line F-H-S3).
-- src:3087 | (2) The Registrar may, upon receipt of any notification referred to
-- src:3088 | in subsection (1) and if satisfied that —
-- src:3090 | (a) the error referred to in subsection (1)(a) is typographical or
-- src:3091 | clerical in nature; or
-- src:3093 | (b) the error referred to in subsection (1)(b) is, in the
-- src:3094 | Registrar’s opinion, unintended and does not prejudice
-- src:3095 | any person,
-- src:3097 | rectify the register accordingly.
@ref s 12C(2) (src:3087-3097)
GIVEN `the Registrar has received a notification referred to in subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the error is the error referred to in subsection (1)(a) and the Registrar is satisfied that it is typographical or clerical in nature` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the error is the error referred to in subsection (1)(b) and the Registrar is satisfied that it is, in the Registrar's opinion, unintended and does not prejudice any person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 12C(2) the Registrar may rectify the register accordingly` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the Registrar has received a notification referred to in subsection (1)`)
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The Registrar may, upon receipt of any notification referred to in subsection (1) and if satisfied that" (a failed "upon": counts as "where", the delegated-defences ruling of 2026-11-05, item (c); split site (ii), fork line F-H-S1)
    ELSE (IF    `the error is the error referred to in subsection (1)(a) and the Registrar is satisfied that it is typographical or clerical in nature`
             OR `the error is the error referred to in subsection (1)(b) and the Registrar is satisfied that it is, in the Registrar's opinion, unintended and does not prejudice any person`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): a grant ("the Registrar may") whose "if satisfied" gate is not met; the grant ruling of 2026-11-12, limit 1 (fork line F-H-S3)

-- src:3101 | (3) In rectifying the register under subsection (2), the Registrar
-- src:3102 | must not expunge any document from the register.
@ref s 12C(3) (src:3101-3102)
GIVEN `the Registrar is rectifying the register under subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 12C(3) the Registrar is barred from expunging a document from the register` MEANS
    IF `the Registrar is rectifying the register under subsection (2)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In rectifying the register under subsection (2), the Registrar must not expunge any document from the register"; the text says nothing of another rectification

-- src:3106 | (4) The decision made by the Registrar on whether to rectify the
-- src:3107 | register under subsection (2) is final.
@ref s 12C(4) (src:3106-3107)
GIVEN `the decision is a decision of the Registrar on whether to rectify the register under subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 12C(4) the Registrar's decision on whether to rectify the register is final` MEANS
    IF `the decision is a decision of the Registrar on whether to rectify the register under subsection (2)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The decision made by the Registrar on whether to rectify the register under subsection (2) is final"; the text says nothing of another decision

§ `Section 12D: rectification or updating on the Registrar's initiative`

-- src:3113 | 12D.—(1) The Registrar may rectify or update any particulars or
-- src:3114 | document in a register kept by him or her, if the Registrar is satisfied
-- src:3115 | that —
-- src:3117 | (a) there is a defect or error in the particulars or document
-- src:3118 | arising from any grammatical, typographical or similar
-- src:3119 | mistake;
-- src:3123 | (aa) the register is inaccurate in respect of the particulars or
-- src:3124 | document, taking account of information given in, or in
-- src:3125 | support of, a notice to the Registrar under section 173A(1)
-- src:3126 | or 173E(1), (2) or (3); or
-- src:3130 | (b) there is evidence of a conflict between the particulars of a
-- src:3131 | company or person and —
-- src:3133 | (i) other information in the register relating to that
-- src:3134 | company or person; or
-- src:3136 | (ii) other information relating to that company or person
-- src:3137 | obtained from such department or Ministry of the
-- src:3142 | Government, or statutory body or other body
-- src:3143 | corporate as may be prescribed, or the courts.
@ref s 12D(1) (src:3113-3143)
GIVEN `the Registrar is satisfied that there is a defect or error in the particulars or document arising from a grammatical, typographical or similar mistake` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Registrar is satisfied that the register is inaccurate in respect of the particulars or document, taking account of information given in, or in support of, a notice to the Registrar under section 173A(1) or 173E(1), (2) or (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Registrar is satisfied that there is evidence of a conflict between the particulars of a company or person and other information in the register relating to that company or person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Registrar is satisfied that there is evidence of a conflict between the particulars of a company or person and other information relating to that company or person obtained from a prescribed department, Ministry, statutory body or other body corporate, or the courts` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 12D(1) the Registrar may rectify or update the particulars or document in the register` MEANS
    IF    `the Registrar is satisfied that there is a defect or error in the particulars or document arising from a grammatical, typographical or similar mistake`
       OR `the Registrar is satisfied that the register is inaccurate in respect of the particulars or document, taking account of information given in, or in support of, a notice to the Registrar under section 173A(1) or 173E(1), (2) or (3)`
       OR `the Registrar is satisfied that there is evidence of a conflict between the particulars of a company or person and other information in the register relating to that company or person`
       OR `the Registrar is satisfied that there is evidence of a conflict between the particulars of a company or person and other information relating to that company or person obtained from a prescribed department, Ministry, statutory body or other body corporate, or the courts`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): a grant ("The Registrar may rectify or update") whose "if the Registrar is satisfied" gate is not met; the grant ruling of 2026-11-12, limit 1 (fork line F-H-S3)

-- src:3149 | (1A) Subsections (2) to (5) do not apply where the Registrar
-- src:3150 | rectifies or updates the register under subsection (1)(aa).
@ref s 12D(1A) (src:3149-3150)
GIVEN `the Registrar rectifies or updates the register under subsection (1)(aa)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 12D(1A) subsections (2) to (5) apply to the rectification or updating` MEANS
    IF `the Registrar rectifies or updates the register under subsection (1)(aa)`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsections (2) to (5) do not apply where the Registrar rectifies or updates the register under subsection (1)(aa)" (a flat negative)
    ELSE NOTHING      -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection says when subsections (2) to (5) do not apply; for a rectification under (1)(a) or (b) they apply by their own terms

-- (2): the notice before rectifying. "except under prescribed circumstances": the circumstances are prescribed outside the sources, so whether they exist is a fact the person states.
-- src:3154 | (2) Before the Registrar rectifies or updates the register under
-- src:3155 | subsection (1), the Registrar must, except under prescribed
-- src:3156 | circumstances, give written notice to the company or person whose
-- src:3157 | documents or particulars are to be rectified or updated of the
-- src:3158 | Registrar’s intention to do so, and state in the notice —
@ref s 12D(2) (src:3154-3158)
GIVEN `the Registrar rectifies or updates the register under subsection (1)(a) or (b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Registrar rectifies or updates the register under subsection (1)(aa)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the circumstances are prescribed circumstances in which written notice need not be given` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 12D(2) the Registrar must give written notice to the company or person before rectifying or updating the register` MEANS
    IF `the Registrar rectifies or updates the register under subsection (1)(aa)`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsections (2) to (5) do not apply where the Registrar rectifies or updates the register under subsection (1)(aa)" (a flat negative, subsection (1A))
    ELSE (IF `the circumstances are prescribed circumstances in which written notice need not be given`
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the Registrar must, except under prescribed circumstances, give written notice" (an exception, met)
          ELSE (IF `the Registrar rectifies or updates the register under subsection (1)(a) or (b)`
                THEN JUST TRUE
                ELSE NOTHING))   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection speaks only of a rectification or updating under subsection (1)

-- (2)(b): "the date by which any written objection ... must be delivered to the Registrar, being a date at least 30 days after the date of the notice": the earliest date that may be stated is the notice date plus 30 days (P1).
-- src:3163 | (b) the date by which any written objection to the proposed
-- src:3164 | rectification or updating must be delivered to the Registrar,
-- src:3165 | being a date at least 30 days after the date of the notice.
@ref s 12D(2)(b) (src:3163-3165)
GIVEN `the date of the notice` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 12D(2)(b) the earliest date that may be stated for delivering a written objection` MEANS
    `period: the last day of a period after` `the date of the notice` 30 Days

-- src:3154 | (2) Before the Registrar rectifies or updates the register under
-- src:3155 | subsection (1), the Registrar must, except under prescribed
-- src:3156 | circumstances, give written notice to the company or person whose
-- src:3157 | documents or particulars are to be rectified or updated of the
-- src:3158 | Registrar’s intention to do so, and state in the notice —
-- src:3160 | (a) the reasons for and details of the proposed rectification or
-- src:3161 | updating to be made to the register; and
-- src:3163 | (b) the date by which any written objection to the proposed
-- src:3164 | rectification or updating must be delivered to the Registrar,
-- src:3165 | being a date at least 30 days after the date of the notice.
@ref s 12D(2) (src:3154-3165)
GIVEN `the notice is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice states the reasons for and details of the proposed rectification or updating to be made to the register` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice states a date by which any written objection to the proposed rectification or updating must be delivered to the Registrar` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date of the notice` IS A DATE
      `the date stated in the notice for delivering a written objection` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 12D(2) the notice has the content and form the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF    `the notice is in writing`
      AND `the notice states the reasons for and details of the proposed rectification or updating to be made to the register`
      AND `the notice states a date by which any written objection to the proposed rectification or updating must be delivered to the Registrar`
      AND `the date stated in the notice for delivering a written objection` AT LEAST `s 12D(2)(b) the earliest date that may be stated for delivering a written objection` `the date of the notice`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "give written notice ..., and state in the notice -- (a) the reasons for and details of the proposed rectification or updating ...; and (b) the date by which any written objection ... must be delivered ..., being a date at least 30 days after the date of the notice" (a duty not met: the provision's own question; marginal reading (a))

-- (3): "may deliver to the Registrar, not later than the date specified under subsection (2)(b), a written objection": a period the text fixes in its own words; outside it JUST FALSE (periods ruling (a)).
-- src:3169 | (3) The company or person notified under subsection (2) may
-- src:3170 | deliver to the Registrar, not later than the date specified under
-- src:3171 | subsection (2)(b), a written objection to the proposed rectification or
-- src:3172 | updating of the register.
@ref s 12D(3) (src:3169-3172)
GIVEN `the company or person was notified under subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the written objection is delivered` IS A DATE
      `the date specified under subsection (2)(b)` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 12D(3) the company or person may deliver a written objection to the proposed rectification or updating` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the company or person was notified under subsection (2)`)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the right is that of "The company or person notified under subsection (2)"; the text says nothing of anyone else
    ELSE (IF `the date the written objection is delivered` AT MOST `the date specified under subsection (2)(b)`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may deliver to the Registrar, not later than the date specified under subsection (2)(b), a written objection" (a period the text fixes in its own words: the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (a))

-- src:3176 | (4) The Registrar must not rectify or update the register if the
-- src:3177 | Registrar receives a written objection under subsection (3) to the
-- src:3178 | proposed rectification or updating by the date specified under
-- src:3179 | subsection (2)(b), unless the Registrar is satisfied that the objection
-- src:3180 | is frivolous or vexatious or has been withdrawn.
@ref s 12D(4) (src:3176-3180)
GIVEN `the Registrar received a written objection under subsection (3) to the proposed rectification or updating by the date specified under subsection (2)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Registrar is satisfied that the objection is frivolous or vexatious` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the objection has been withdrawn` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 12D(4) the Registrar is barred from rectifying or updating the register` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the Registrar received a written objection under subsection (3) to the proposed rectification or updating by the date specified under subsection (2)(b)`)
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The Registrar must not rectify or update the register if the Registrar receives a written objection under subsection (3) ... by the date specified" (a failed "if" of a bar: the provision's own question; marginal reading (a); subsection (5) is the other limb)
    ELSE (IF `the Registrar is satisfied that the objection is frivolous or vexatious` OR `the objection has been withdrawn`
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the Registrar is satisfied that the objection is frivolous or vexatious or has been withdrawn" (an "unless", met)
          ELSE JUST TRUE)

-- src:3184 | (5) The Registrar may rectify or update the register if the Registrar
-- src:3185 | does not receive a written objection under subsection (3) by the date
-- src:3186 | specified under subsection (2)(b).
@ref s 12D(5) (src:3184-3186)
GIVEN `the Registrar did not receive a written objection under subsection (3) by the date specified under subsection (2)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 12D(5) the Registrar may rectify or update the register` MEANS
    IF `the Registrar did not receive a written objection under subsection (3) by the date specified under subsection (2)(b)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): a grant ("The Registrar may rectify or update the register") whose "if" gate is not met; the grant ruling of 2026-11-12, limit 1 (fork line F-H-S3); subsection (4) governs an objection received

-- src:3190 | (6) The Registrar may include such notation as the Registrar thinks
-- src:3191 | fit on the register for the purposes of providing information relating to
-- src:3192 | any error, defect or inaccuracy in any particulars or document in the
@ref s 12D(6) (src:3190-3192)
GIVEN `the notation provides information relating to an error, defect or inaccuracy in particulars or a document in the register` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 12D(6) the Registrar may include the notation on the register` MEANS
    IF `the notation provides information relating to an error, defect or inaccuracy in particulars or a document in the register`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the Registrar may include "such notation as the Registrar thinks fit ... for the purposes of providing information relating to any error, defect or inaccuracy"; the text says nothing of a notation for another purpose

-- src:3197 | register, and may remove such notation if the Registrar is satisfied
-- src:3198 | that it no longer serves any useful purpose.
@ref s 12D(6) (src:3197-3198)
GIVEN `the Registrar is satisfied that the notation no longer serves any useful purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 12D(6) the Registrar may remove the notation` MEANS
    IF `the Registrar is satisfied that the notation no longer serves any useful purpose`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may remove such notation if the Registrar is satisfied that it no longer serves any useful purpose"; an "if" gate on a grant (fork line F-H-S3)

-- src:3204 | (7) Despite anything in this section, the Registrar may, if the
-- src:3205 | Registrar is satisfied that there is any error, defect or inaccuracy in
-- src:3206 | any particulars or document in a register, by written notice, request
-- src:3207 | that the company to which the particulars or document relate, or its
-- src:3208 | officers take such steps within such time as the Registrar may specify
-- src:3209 | to ensure that the error, defect or inaccuracy is rectified.
@ref s 12D(7) (src:3204-3209)
GIVEN `the Registrar is satisfied that there is an error, defect or inaccuracy in particulars or a document in a register` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 12D(7) the Registrar may by written notice request the company or its officers to take steps within a time the Registrar specifies` MEANS
    IF `the Registrar is satisfied that there is an error, defect or inaccuracy in particulars or a document in a register`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the Registrar may, if the Registrar is satisfied that there is any error, defect or inaccuracy ..., by written notice, request"; an "if" gate on a grant (fork line F-H-S3)

§ `Regulative rules of ss 12B to 12D`

DECLARE `s 12B to 12D act` IS ONE OF
    `s 12B(1) rectify the register on receipt of the Court's order`
    `s 12B(2) file the fresh document with a copy of the Court order and a copy of the Court application`
    `s 12C(3) expunge a document from the register in rectifying it under subsection (2)`
    `s 12D(2) give written notice of the intention to rectify or update the register`
    `s 12D(4) rectify or update the register despite a written objection under subsection (3)`

-- No time limit and no consequence the text states: no breach path (NOTES.md, Rules with no breach path).
-- src:3056 | 12B.—(1) Where it appears to the Court, as a result of evidence
-- src:3057 | adduced before it by an applicant company, that any particular
-- src:3058 | recorded in a register is erroneous or defective, the Court may, by
-- src:3059 | order, direct the Registrar to rectify the register on such terms and
-- src:3060 | conditions as seem to the Court just and expedient, as are specified in
-- src:3061 | the order and the Registrar must, upon receipt of the order, rectify the
-- src:3062 | register accordingly.
@ref s 12B(1) (src:3056-3062)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 12B to 12D act`
`s 12B(1) the Registrar must rectify the register on receipt of the order` MEANS
    PARTY Registrar
    MUST `s 12B(1) rectify the register on receipt of the Court's order`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    -- no LEST: s 12B(1) states no time for this duty, so a breach needs a standard from elsewhere (Interpretation Act 1965 s 52: "with all convenient speed"); dropped clause: LEST BREACH BY Registrar BECAUSE "the Registrar did not rectify the register on receipt of the Court's order" (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md)

-- src:3066 | (2) An order of the Court made under subsection (1) may require
-- src:3067 | that a fresh document, showing the rectification, must be filed by the
-- src:3068 | applicant company with the Registrar together with a copy of the
-- src:3069 | Court order, and a copy of the Court application.
@ref s 12B(2) (src:3066-3069)
GIVEN `the name of the applicant company` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 12B to 12D act`
`s 12B(2) the applicant company must file the fresh document` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the applicant company`
    MUST `s 12B(2) file the fresh document with a copy of the Court order and a copy of the Court application`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    -- no LEST: s 12B(2) states no time for this duty, so a breach needs a standard from elsewhere (Interpretation Act 1965 s 52: "with all convenient speed"); dropped clause: LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the applicant company` BECAUSE "the applicant company did not file the fresh document the Court's order required" (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md)

-- The prohibition of s 12C(3): the text names the bearer (the Registrar) and the act (expunging a document): a trace in which the act occurs is BREACH.
-- src:3101 | (3) In rectifying the register under subsection (2), the Registrar
-- src:3102 | must not expunge any document from the register.
@ref s 12C(3) (src:3101-3102)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 12B to 12D act`
`s 12C(3) the Registrar must not expunge any document from the register` MEANS
    PARTY Registrar
    SHANT `s 12C(3) expunge a document from the register in rectifying it under subsection (2)`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Registrar BECAUSE "the Registrar expunged a document from the register in rectifying it under subsection (2)"

-- src:3154 | (2) Before the Registrar rectifies or updates the register under
-- src:3155 | subsection (1), the Registrar must, except under prescribed
-- src:3156 | circumstances, give written notice to the company or person whose
-- src:3157 | documents or particulars are to be rectified or updated of the
-- src:3158 | Registrar’s intention to do so, and state in the notice —
@ref s 12D(2) (src:3154-3158)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 12B to 12D act`
`s 12D(2) the Registrar must give written notice before rectifying or updating the register` MEANS
    PARTY Registrar
    MUST `s 12D(2) give written notice of the intention to rectify or update the register`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    -- no LEST: s 12D(2) states no time for this duty, so a breach needs a standard from elsewhere (Interpretation Act 1965 s 52: "with all convenient speed"); dropped clause: LEST BREACH BY Registrar BECAUSE "the Registrar did not give written notice of the intention to rectify or update the register" (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md)

-- src:3176 | (4) The Registrar must not rectify or update the register if the
-- src:3177 | Registrar receives a written objection under subsection (3) to the
-- src:3178 | proposed rectification or updating by the date specified under
-- src:3179 | subsection (2)(b), unless the Registrar is satisfied that the objection
-- src:3180 | is frivolous or vexatious or has been withdrawn.
@ref s 12D(4) (src:3176-3180)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 12B to 12D act`
`s 12D(4) the Registrar must not rectify or update the register despite a written objection` MEANS
    PARTY Registrar
    SHANT `s 12D(4) rectify or update the register despite a written objection under subsection (3)`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Registrar BECAUSE "the Registrar rectified or updated the register despite a written objection received by the date specified"
